					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jacob-conwell" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1372582); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1372582&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606250468" alt="Jacob Conwell" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1372582)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jacob-conwell" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1372582); return false;" >Jacob Conwell</a></span> <span class="odate time_1507387967 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">07 Oct 2017 14:52</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3609186">
									

<p>I really dig this for a variety of reasons.</p>
<p>First off, it feels like a nice continuation of the relationship you established AR and MC&amp;D having in 2987, which is great world building.</p>
<p>Second, I feel you do a great job with how Anderson himself would approach this request from MC&amp;D. That initial hesitation, followed by him realizing what exactly MC&amp;D is requesting possession bots for, and jumping on board is 100% in character.</p>
<p>Finally, and I'm going to hide this cause its spoliers:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I was blind sided by the twist ending, where Mr. Jefferson himself was a robot the whole time. Considering how a running trope in the Anderson series is people turning out to be robots all along, this really did a good job of holding the punch until the very end.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>+1 Cimmerian.</p>
<p>And the Blade Runner reference in the title is A+</p>

